{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789853460,"nonce":"PPjWsCi8mlpfIZQjC9Jb02xVzjQ=","title":"a bound method of a runtime-mapped extern class has no closure","message":"`var f = m.keys; f()` for `m:Map\u003cString,Int\u003e` (or a `haxe.ds.StringMap`) lowers to nothing: `lower_method_reference` finds the method in neither `function_map` nor `external_function_map` because `keys` is a runtime mapping row, not a compiled function, so there is no thunk to close over. `Lambda.array({ iterator : h.keys })` (TestBasetypes, three times) therefore iterates nothing. The closure needs a thunk that calls the mapped runtime symbol with the captured receiver.","files":null}]}